{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016pm8n6s2CshUUk1BfchsMr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, built as a self-contained Python web app. Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose:** It's a GTD-style task/project manager whose source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, plus archives like `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) â€” no database, no binary formats, designed to stay readable/editable from any CLI or editor.\n\n- **What it ships (core):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a stdlib-only HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on each request and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`. `anchor_gui.py` is the project's one declared deliverable.\n\n- **Task lifecycle:** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each optionally carrying notes; all edits are logged to daily `logs/` files.\n\n- **Self-testing:** A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, via Task Scheduler) parses every file, boots a throwaway server on a test port, exercises every endpoint and state transition, and writes a report â€” surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **The major build effort layered on top â€” an \"R&D control surface\" (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\"):** turns each project's window into a mission-control cockpit for trio-driven R&D (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build, plus Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one status light (green/amber/red/grey); clicking expands an **inline panel** with a cached summary on top and a real, resizable terminal below.\n\n- **What makes the cockpit real:** persistent **ConPTY terminals** (the lone permitted native dependency, `pywinpty`, lazy-loaded in `pty_manager.py` only), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, durable session/registry state under `.anchor/`, proactive cached AI summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter, via a stubbable runner seam), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), and type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port hard-guarded â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render).\n\n- **Branding/scope:** Presented as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"; everything lives in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), Python 3.8+ stdlib-only except that single terminal extra.\n\n**Status:** v4 \"Project Cockpit\" is built (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) and merged to master; the current branch `foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit` is iterating on a v4.1 rebuild of the project window to match the \"Paradigm-2\" mockup."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24766,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24766},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3a280d1-0b31-4b08-b090-67f9261f414a","uuid":"1a012641-a321-43b3-a694-62057c3ebc7b","request_id":"req_011Cc2HgyuxQt3gkKmZZfLvg"}
